 35CL3cDP Particle decay is assumed to populate only the ground state of the    
 35CL4cDP daughter nucleus based on the following considerations: (1)           
 35CL5cDP Transitions to excited states in the final nucleus would require log  
 35CL6cDP {Ift} values above those of the superallowed T=2 state at 6.61 MeV in 
 35CL7cDP {+36}Ar. (2) If the first excited state were populated in particle    
 35CL8cDP decay, a (probably stronger) peak at higher energy corresponding to   
 35CL9cDP ground-state decay should be observable, provided the ratio of        
 35CLAcDP penetrabilities is sufficiently large. Proton and |a-particle         
 35CLBcDP penetrabilities have been calculated for all observed transitions.    
 35CLCcDP When the penetrability ratio exceeds a factor of 100, a stronger      
 35CLDcDP ground-state transition should be observable. No such characteristic  
 35CLEcDP pairs of particle groups have been found in the present spectra.      
